    <item>
      <title>Solved: Class Inheritance Issues in Python 3.7 Dataclasses</title>
      <link>https://sqlpey.com/python/solved-class-inheritance-python-3-7-dataclasses/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 15 Nov 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://sqlpey.com/python/solved-class-inheritance-python-3-7-dataclasses/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;solved-class-inheritance-issues-in-python-37-dataclasses&#34;&gt;Solved: Class Inheritance Issues in Python 3.7 Dataclasses&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If you&amp;rsquo;re working with Python&amp;rsquo;s dataclasses, you&amp;rsquo;ve likely come across issues when trying to implement inheritance in your class structures. One common problem arises when you attempt to have default parameters in your parent class while defining non-default parameters in a child class — this can lead to errors like &lt;code&gt;TypeError: non-default argument &#39;school&#39; follows default argument&lt;/code&gt;. This comprehensive guide will explore different approaches to tackle this issue effectively.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Solved: How to Fix Class Inheritance Issues in Python 3.7 Dataclasses</title>
      <link>https://sqlpey.com/python/solved-how-to-fix-class-inheritance-issues-in-python-3-7-dataclasses/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 15 Nov 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://sqlpey.com/python/solved-how-to-fix-class-inheritance-issues-in-python-3-7-dataclasses/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;ve been diving into the intricacies of using dataclass constructions introduced in Python 3.7, particularly how to manage class inheritance effectively. A challenge I faced revolved around the improper handling of argument order when subclassing—namely, a boolean parameter in the child class being incorrectly positioned. This misalignment inevitably leads to a &lt;code&gt;TypeError&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Here&amp;rsquo;s an excerpt of my initial attempt implementing class inheritance:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-python&#34; data-lang=&#34;python&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; dataclasses &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; dataclass&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;@dataclass&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Parent&lt;/span&gt;:&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    name: str&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    age: int&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    ugly: bool &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;False&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;print_name&lt;/span&gt;(self):&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        print(self&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;name)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;print_age&lt;/span&gt;(self):&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        print(self&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;age)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;print_id&lt;/span&gt;(self):&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        print(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;The Name is &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;self&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;name&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt; and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;self&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;name&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt; is &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;self&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;age&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt; years old&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;@dataclass&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Child&lt;/span&gt;(Parent):&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    school: str&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    ugly: bool &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;True&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;jack &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; Parent(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;jack snr&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;32&lt;/span&gt;, ugly&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;True&lt;/span&gt;)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;jack_son &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; Child(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;jack jnr&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;12&lt;/span&gt;, school&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;harvard&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;, ugly&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;True&lt;/span&gt;)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;jack&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;print_id()&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;jack_son&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;print_id()&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Upon executing this code, I encountered the following error message:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Top 7 Methods to Set Values in Frozen Dataclass Post Initialization</title>
      <link>https://sqlpey.com/python/top-7-methods-to-set-values-in-frozen-dataclass-post-initialization/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 15 Nov 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://sqlpey.com/python/top-7-methods-to-set-values-in-frozen-dataclass-post-initialization/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;When working with Python&amp;rsquo;s frozen dataclasses, one may encounter challenges when attempting to set a field&amp;rsquo;s value in the &lt;code&gt;__post_init__&lt;/code&gt; method due to the immutability enforced by the &lt;code&gt;frozen=True&lt;/code&gt; setting. Is it possible to derive values for fields during initialization while maintaining the frozen constraints? Let&amp;rsquo;s dive into several methodical approaches to tackle this issue.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;exploring-possible-solutions-to-set-values-in-frozen-dataclasses&#34;&gt;Exploring Possible Solutions to Set Values in Frozen Dataclasses&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;h4 id=&#34;problem-overview&#34;&gt;Problem Overview&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The primary issue arises when you attempt to assign values to fields in a frozen dataclass directly within &lt;code&gt;__post_init__&lt;/code&gt;, which leads to a &lt;code&gt;FrozenInstanceError&lt;/code&gt;. The following code snippet illustrates a potential frozen dataclass that encounters this issue when trying to set the &lt;code&gt;value&lt;/code&gt; based on the &lt;code&gt;rank&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
